  "summary": "This study fabricated LiF/HCl-etched Ti3C2Tx and hydrazine-reduced RGO films by vacuum-assisted filtration, followed by dry transfer onto prestrained VHB elastomer. Five composition endpoints were fabricated: pure Ti3C2Tx, Ti3C2Tx/RGO with 25, 50, and 75 wt% RGO, and pure RGO; only pure Ti3C2Tx, 50 wt% RGO composite, and pure RGO received reported electrochemical characterization. The headline 50 wt% RGO Ti3C2Tx/RGO electrode achieved 49 mF/cm2 (~490 F/cm3 and ~140 F/g) in 1 M H2SO4, with Figure 6 specifying GCD comparison at 1 A/g. Mass loading, BET area, pore metrics, porosity, and XRD interlayer spacings were not reported."
